␀Y ␀. ␀    ␀Yes␀ No␀Í␀n/a␀
 MORE   (Esc stops Pausing, Ctrl-C stops Completely, any other Continues)␀ MORE                                                                    
␀                                                                               ␀Error! Need Support File ␀SYNTAX: USBUHCI [Options]

  /?      Í Show this HELP screen
  /A      Í Show all ALIASES for these command line Options
  /ErrLvl Í Show all ErrorLevels (DOS Return Codes)
  /U      Í UNINSTALL from memory
  /L:Y|N  Í Force installation into LOW memory (default = No)

  /Index #       Í Use UHCI Host with PCI INDEX # (default = 0)
  /IOAddr #      Í Use I/O base ADDR # (100h-FFE0h, divisible by 32)
  /IRQ #         Í Use IRQ # (3-15, default = 9)
  /DisableLegacy Í Disable Legacy Keyboard/Mouse support
  /DisableOther  Í Disable Other Control program
  /P:#           Í Pause # deciSeconds before finding Root Devices (0-255)
  /Beep:Y|N      Í BEEP Speaker when bad Device is found (default = Yes)
  /PD[:#]        Í Display Program Debug messages during install and uninstall
                      # = Milliseconds to delay each step (0-2000, default = 0)

  /Run #     Í Run (Resume/Enable) Device Address # ¿
  /Stop #    Í Stop (Disable) Device Address #      ´  0-1   = Host/Root Hub
  /Reset #   Í Reset Device Address #               ´  2-127 = Attached Dvc
  /Suspend # Í Suspend Device Address #             ´128-255 = All Hosts
  /Resume #  Í Resume (not Enable) Device Address # Ù

  /PowerOn #    Í Power On Device Address #    ¿
  /PowerOff #   Í Power Off Device Address #   ´ 2-127
  /PowerReset # Í Power Reset Device Address # Ù

  /SC:D# C# Í Set Configuration of Device D# (2-127) to value C# (0-255)
  /RW:# Y|N Í Enable/disable Remote Wakeup on Device # (2-127)
  /TM:# Y|N Í Enable/disable Test Mode on Device # (2-127)

  /Timing #    Í Set Timing to # Bits/Frame (11936-12063, default = 12000)
  /Debug, /SST Í Debug/SingleStep the Host

  /Host       Í Show Status of Host (PCI/USB/Root Hub)
  /FL         Í Show Status of Frame List
  /QH         Í Show Status of Queue Heads
  /TD [#]     Í Show Status of Transfer Descriptor(s), optional Idx # (0-255)
  /AD         Í Show Status of Addressed Devices
  /ND         Í Show Status of New Device Notification Entries
  /Descr [:#] Í Show Descriptors for Device Address # (2-127)
                   If no Address is provided, shows Last Enumerated Device
  /R A# I#    Í Show HID Report Descr for Dvc Addr A# (2-127), Intf I# (0-255)

  /RB Í Reset all Bad Devices on all Hosts␀      FRAME LIST ENTRIES
